I started 2012 as a road-bike noob on a test ride. By the end of 2014 I had a few century rides behind me, two Levi&rsquo;s GranFondos out of Santa Rosa, a windy coast ride in Maui, eight days of a Rapha Festive 500, and a relaxed finish at Foxy&rsquo;s Fall Century.
This is a look back at those three years, built from the posts and photos I shared at the time. I already wrote up my first century, the Mount Hamilton Loop, in April 2013.
2012: a test ride, then longer days # On April 28 I posted a photo from a test ride: &ldquo;road bike noob&hellip;test drive:)&rdquo; A week later, on May 7, I bought my first bike helmet.
The rides got longer as the year went on. On June 2 I was still out with &ldquo;another 18 miles to go back:)&rdquo; On September 23 I did a &ldquo;Sunday easy ride&rdquo; of 41 miles and 1,798 ft (about 66 km and 548 m), and joked that it was the price of eating 雞排: &ldquo;這是吃了雞排的代價&hellip;LOL&rdquo;
April 28, 2012: “road bike noob&hellip;test drive:)” Levi&rsquo;s GranFondo 2012: the Medio route # On September 29 I rode Levi&rsquo;s GranFondo in Santa Rosa, on the Medio route: 65 miles and 3,500 ft (about 105 km and 1,067 m). When I signed up I wrote, &ldquo;Registered Levi&rsquo;s GranFondo - Medio 65 miles 3500 feet:)&rdquo;
A public Medio route on Ride with GPS is still up; that page is labeled as the 2011 course, so the line may not match the 2012 ride exactly.
The day started early: &ldquo;It is 5am:)&rdquo; Along the way I passed the ocean on Highway 1 — &ldquo;Pacific Ocean @ Hw1&rdquo; — and stopped to eat: &ldquo;Another rest stop&hellip;I am full:)&rdquo; Then the road tilted up. &ldquo;Now&hellip;I know why there is a rest stop&hellip;the 10% is ahead(◎_◎;)&rdquo; I also posted &ldquo;The wall:)&rdquo; and, later, &ldquo;climbing is not so fun:)&rdquo; At some point there were &ldquo;Another 40 miles to go:)&rdquo;
The Scott I rode that day, with number 7225. &ldquo;Pacific Ocean @ Hw1.&rdquo; A rest stop in the fog — &ldquo;Another rest stop&hellip;I am full:)&rdquo; &ldquo;The wall:)&rdquo; And afterward, in the GranFondo jersey.
Late 2012, and a trip to Maui # In mid-October I was looking for a buddy to ride to Lick Observatory on Mount Hamilton, a 39.9-mile route with 5,944 ft of climbing (about 64 km and 1,812 m). On November 2 I was &ldquo;going to do a 75 miles ride this time:)&rdquo; (about 121 km). On December 9 I did a &ldquo;Sunday Mt. Diablo Ride.(strong wind and cold)&rdquo; with 3,927 ft of elevation gain (about 1,197 m).
Maui, December 2012 # On November 18 I had been thinking about cycling up Haleakalā while on vacation in Maui — 36 miles uphill, from sea level to 10,000 ft (about 58 km and 3,048 m). On December 13 I shared the route I had in mind, &ldquo;Tour de Maui Stage2&rdquo;: Ocean to Haleakalā Summit from Paia, 35.7 miles and 10,208 ft of climbing (about 57.5 km and 3,111 m). It looked too hard at the time, so I didn&rsquo;t ride up. Instead I rode a stretch of the coast, in a strong wind, and my mom picked me up.
On December 16 I posted the bike I rode in Maui: &ldquo;My ride in Maui&hellip;This is $3000 carbon bike:)&rdquo; It was a rental — &ldquo;租的 $40 per day&rdquo; — and, as I wrote in the comments, &ldquo;It is handmade in Taiwan.&rdquo;
The rental bike I rode in Maui: “This is $3000 carbon bike:)” “It is handmade in Taiwan.” “租的 $40 per day.” A few days later I was on the coast. The wind was fierce: &ldquo;好強的風啊〜&rdquo; and &ldquo;風太強&hellip;&rdquo; I couldn&rsquo;t ride back, and my mom came to get me: &ldquo;風太強騎不回去..老媽道路救援：）&rdquo; I also wrote, &ldquo;這個季節不太適合騎那段&hellip;落山風有點恐佈&hellip;左右夾擊&hellip;&rdquo; — this wasn&rsquo;t a good season for that stretch; the 落山風 was a bit terrifying, coming at me from both sides.
The rental bike at a rocky beach, then two stops along the coast: “好強的風啊〜” and “風太強&hellip;”
December 20 was my last day: &ldquo;Going to enjoy my last day in Maui&hellip;biking to the north:)&rdquo; The weather was better — &ldquo;Alright&hellip;I am still in Maui. Nice weather:)&rdquo; — and I posted &ldquo;Nice MTB path&hellip;LOL&rdquo; and &ldquo;Back to sunny beach:)&rdquo; One of the stops was Lahaina.
“Nice MTB path&hellip;LOL” “Back to sunny beach:)” And the bike beside a Lahaina sign.
On December 23 we drove up to Haleakalā. The photos I posted, all captioned &ldquo;Haleakala Crater,&rdquo; are from that drive.
December 23, 2012, from the drive up: “Haleakala Crater.” The summit road, and the view above the clouds.
I did ride up Haleakalā later, in 2018. That&rsquo;s a story for another post.
2013: centuries, climbing, and a new bike # 2013 picked up quickly. On February 7 I posted &ldquo;Century ride!&rdquo; On February 9 I climbed Sierra Road: &ldquo;Complete Climbing Sierra Rd today…Satisifed. 完成6公里平均10%的陡坡&rdquo;
A week later, on February 16, I had a new climbing record: 5,594 ft over 47 miles. I also wrote it as 1,700 m and 75 km: &ldquo;My new record! total 5,594ft elevation 47miles / 新記錄&hellip;爬了1700公尺 75公里&rdquo;
In April I wrote up my first century, the Mount Hamilton Loop. On April 7 I hit 2,000 miles and figured it was time for a new chain: &ldquo;2000 miles&hellip;該換鏈了&rdquo;
April 7, 2013: “2000 miles&hellip;該換鏈了” On May 5 I said goodbye to the bike I had been riding: &ldquo;Thanks to my bike! You have served me well! I am going to upgrade you&hellip;&rdquo;
By June 9, since the start of 2013, I had ridden 1,474 miles (2,372 km) and climbed 94,836 ft (28,906 m).
On August 17 I was looking at &ldquo;last 10 miles..another 2000ft to climb,&rdquo; and then: &ldquo;Thanks to the cloud / I complete the 9 hours ride with total 93 miles/9,100 ft / 今天總共 騎了150公里 爬了2,700公尺&rdquo; On August 31 I posted &ldquo;My 3rd century ride this year.&rdquo;
Levi&rsquo;s GranFondo 2013: the Gran route # On October 5 I went back to Levi&rsquo;s GranFondo, this time on the Gran route. The rest stops I shared were:
20 mi: Monte Rio 30 mi: Cazadero 45 mi: King Ridge 55 mi: Ritchey Ranch 75 mi: Portuguese Beach 80 mi: Coleman Valley (water only) 85 mi: Occidental The 2013 route map, with rest stops marked along the Gran course. A first flat, and the rest of 2013 # On October 19, riding with friends, I had &ldquo;My first flat tire after 2800 miles.&rdquo;
October 19, 2013, with friends: “My first flat tire after 2800 miles.” On December 1 I added up the year so far: &ldquo;so far in 2013, I rode total 3,130miles and up 212,802ft 今年目前總共騎了5,037公里 爬了64,862公尺— feeling accomplished.&rdquo;
Sometime in mid-December I did a Garmin VIRB test ride on Calaveras. Another day that month I wrote, &ldquo;late today&hellip;only did 50.53 mi&hellip;下星期一定要完成120公里的目標:)&rdquo; (50.53 miles is about 81 km.)
Rapha Festive 500, December 2013 # From December 24 onward I joined the Rapha Festive 500: &ldquo;8 days of fun #festive500.&rdquo; I finished with 314 miles (about 505 km).
Day 1 was 100 km, past Pulgas Water Temple and San Andreas Lake. Day 2 was Christmas: &ldquo;Merry Christmas! 公休一日.&rdquo; Day 3 was another 100 km, past Sunol Water Temple, the Alameda Creek Trail, and Old Mission San Jose. Day 4 followed the Coyote Creek Bike Trail to Anderson Dam; I &ldquo;tried to lose some of holiday weight.&rdquo; Day 5 was Tomales Bay.
“8 days of fun #festive500.” Day 1, 100 km: the reflecting pool at Pulgas Water Temple, a stop at San Andreas Lake, and the temple itself.
Day 3 at Old Mission San Jose; Day 4 at Anderson Dam; and Day 5, Tomales Bay.
2014: 5,000 miles, and a relaxed last century # On January 10 I shared a blog post titled &ldquo;Century a Week.&rdquo; On March 9 I hit a new milestone: &ldquo;My first 5,000 miles — in Mount Diablo.&rdquo; (5,000 miles is about 8,047 km.)
March 9, 2014: “My first 5,000 miles — in Mount Diablo.” On May 10 I did my first century of the year: &ldquo;My first century this year. Total: 103 miles(166公里)/5,049ft(1,538公尺). The climbs are ok, but the strong wind almost killed me:)&rdquo; A few days later, on May 15, I ate too much at a BBQ and joked that I needed another century that weekend.
On July 15 I signed up for the Santa Cruz Mountains Challenge 100M, with a note to myself: &ldquo;Need to lose 2-3lbs this week!&rdquo;
On October 18 I rode my last century of the year: &ldquo;My last century this year&hellip;It is very enjoyable, relaxed ride!&rdquo; That was the 2014 Foxy&rsquo;s Fall Century, near Saint Helena and Putah Creek.
Foxy&rsquo;s Fall Century, October 18, 2014: on the road, crossing a graffiti-covered bridge, and riding with others. &ldquo;It is very enjoyable, relaxed ride!&rdquo;
On December 6 I was back on the bike after a break: &ldquo;幾個禮拜沒騎車 好喘！&rdquo; And on December 28, at 新竹市十七公里海岸風景區 in Hsinchu, Taiwan, I posted a road bike on the coast with the caption &ldquo;New buddy!&rdquo; That was the second day of a nine-day Giant tour around the island, which I wrote up in Cycling Around Taiwan, 2014–2015.
December 6, 2014: “幾個禮拜沒騎車 好喘！” December 28, 2014, at 新竹市十七公里海岸風景區: “New buddy!”
